triage: fix_tests: Replaying the scenario gives 7 cards in the draw pile, which is what the game reports. Starting from 10: in round 1 seat 1 TAKEs the offered 2 (no draw) and seat 2 DRAWs one card (9 left); in round 2 both players DRAW (7 left). The test's expected 6 counts one draw too many, while the game's final slots (seat 1 c1=7, c2 empty, c3=3) show the take, the pair shed and the empty slot handled correctly.
